GIMP Palette
Name: Puzzle — Candy Reef
Columns: 6
#
# Direction: sunlit shallows. The one palette here allowed to be loud, because
# a match-3 board is the one screen where colour is not decoration but the
# entire mechanic.
#
# Six gem hues, each two steps: a body and a lighter face. Two steps rather
# than a full ramp is the deliberate part — a 40px gem shaded across five
# values reads as a sphere, and forty spheres read as noise. Flat body plus one
# highlight keeps each gem a *token* you match, not an object you inspect.
#
# The hues are spaced roughly evenly around the wheel and separated by value as
# well as hue, so the board still parses for the ~8% of players who cannot
# separate the red and the green by hue alone.
#
# deep-* is cool and desaturated for the same reason the gems are not: the
# board must never be the thing your eye lands on.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 26  38  58	deep-0-bg
 44  64  94	deep-1
 70 100 138	deep-2
116 156 196	deep-3-tile
232  60  84	gem-red
255 150 166	gem-red-lite
250 148  40	gem-orange
255 204 128	gem-orange-lite
244 226  70	gem-yellow
